The session-scoped pytest fixture named `ta` returns a `TestEnvironmentAccess`, which has already set up all ports as configured. Since the fixture is session-scoped, the ports are only set up once per pytest session. However, it is still possible to control the ports later during testing.

In the following example, a fixture is defined that stops and disconnects a MAPort named `"Model"`, then reconnects it to ensure the application is freshly downloaded in every case.

Note: This example does not include error handling and is not suitable for real-world use. Downloading and starting a simulation application might be a long-running operation, which should not be repeated unconditionally for a single test.

```
@pytest.fixture
def restart_model(ta: TestEnvironmentAccess):
  """Restart the port named 'Model'."""
  # stop and disconnect, if started and connected
  if ta.ports.Model.state >= PortState.STARTED:
    ta.ports.Model.stop()
  if ta.ports.Model.state >= PortState.CONNECTED:

